    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32885" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ōrātus</span></b> ,
		ūs (only in <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>abl. sing.</i> and
			plur.), 
			m.
			oro, <i>a praying</i>, <i>entreating; a request</i>, <i>entreaty</i> (very
			rare but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oratu tuo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Fl. 37, 92</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illarum oratu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. 2, 2, 17</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 9, 14 <i>init.</i></span></i>: magnis oratibus, Coripp. Laud. <i><span class="en">Just. 2,
			4</span></i>.</div>
